### **2. FUZZY MATCHING: WHERE AND HOW**

**Threshold:** `0.72` (defined at line 41 of `requisicao-logic.ts`)

#### **Fuzzy Match Implementation**

The actual fuzzy matching happens **in the frontend**, not in the edge function. The edge function returns the AI-parsed items; the frontend then enriches them against the catalog.

**File:** `C:\Users\olive_\OneDrive\Documentos\codigo\Momma\momma-stock-insight\src\pages\requisicao-logic.ts` (Lines 162–256)

```typescript
export const MATCH_THRESHOLD = 0.72;

export function enrichItemsWithCatalog(
  items: AIProcessedItem[],
  catalog: CatalogProduct[],
  threshold: number = MATCH_THRESHOLD,
  aliases: AliasEntry[] = []
): EnrichmentResult {
  // Priority:
  // 1) Already locked → keep
  // 2) Exact name match
  // 3) Alias (learned) match
  // 4) Fuzzy similarity

  for (const item of items) {
    // ...
    if (!match) {
      let bestMatch: CatalogProduct | null = null;
      let bestSim = 0;
      for (const p of catalog) {
        const sim = similarity(item.name, p.nome);  // <-- FUZZY CALL
        if (sim > bestSim) {
          bestSim = sim;
          bestMatch = p;
        }
      }
      if (bestMatch && bestSim >= threshold) {
        match = bestMatch;
        bestScore = bestSim;
        matchSource = 'fuzzy';
      }
    }
    // ...
  }
}
```

#### **The `similarity()` Function (Levenshtein-based)**

**File:** `C:\Users\olive_\OneDrive\Documentos\codigo\Momma\momma-stock-insight\src\shared\lib\stringUtils.ts` (Lines 79–88)

```typescript
export const similarity = (a: string, b: string): number => {
  const na = normalizeName(a);
  const nb = normalizeName(b);
  if (!na || !nb) return 0;
  const dist = levenshtein(na, nb);
  const maxLen = Math.max(na.length, nb.length);
  const baseScore = 1 - dist / maxLen;
  const substrBonus = (na.includes(nb) || nb.includes(na)) ? 0.1 : 0;
  return Math.max(0, Math.min(1, baseScore + substrBonus));
};
```

**Key algorithm:**
1. Both strings are normalized (lowercase, no accents, alphanumeric only)
2. Levenshtein distance is computed
3. Score = `1 - (distance / max_length)`
4. **+0.1 bonus** if one is a substring of the other
5. Result clamped to [0, 1]

**What is being matched:** Just the AI-extracted `item.name` string against catalog product names. **NOT** combining with header/category context.

#### **Frontend Requisition Integration**

**File:** `C:\Users\olive_\OneDrive\Documentos\codigo\Momma\momma-stock-insight\src\features\requisicoes\ui\Requisicao.page.tsx` (Lines 2567–2609)

The frontend calls this **after** receiving items from the edge function:

```typescript
for (const item of allProcessedItems) {
  // 1. Tentar encontrar por Alias aprendido
  const learnedProductId = findProductByAlias(item.name);

  if (learnedProductId) {
    const learnedProduct = activeProducts.find(p => p.id === learnedProductId);
    if (learnedProduct) {
      bestMatch = learnedProduct;
      bestScore = 1.0;
    }
  }

  // 2. Se não achou por alias, tentar fuzzy matching
  if (!bestMatch) {
    for (const product of activeProducts) {
      const score = similarity(item.name, product.nome);
      if (score > bestScore) {
        bestScore = score;
        bestMatch = product;
      }
    }
  }

  const MATCH_THRESHOLD = 0.72;

  if (bestMatch && bestScore >= MATCH_THRESHOLD) {
    processedItems.push({
      ...item,
      name: bestMatch.nome,  // <-- Overwrites AI output!
      matchedId: bestMatch.id.toString(),
      matchConfidence: bestScore,
      originalName: item.name,
      code: (bestMatch as any).codigo_interno,
      isLocked: true
    });
  } else {
    // Item goes to review
    lowConfidenceItems.push({...item, isLowConfidence: true});
  }
}
```

**Critical issue here:** The fuzzy match is applied **only to `item.name`** (the AI's extracted product name), NOT to a combined "header + item" string.

